# The storefront signs each shopper's address with this secret, and a valid signature is believed first. Set the same value
# (32 characters or more) on the storefront. With it set, requests that come through the storefront need neither setting below.
CLIENT_ADDRESS_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Who is the client for anything not signed? Used by the storefront API rate limits (D-081). Set at most one of the two. With neither, the
# address of the connection is used, which behind the storefront's BFF is the storefront server: every shopper would
# then share one limit. x-forwarded-for is never trusted without this setting.

# How many proxies in front of this backend append to x-forwarded-for. The storefront's BFF counts as one: it sends the
# shopper's address as x-forwarded-for. So 1 when the storefront connects straight to this backend, 2 with a load
# balancer between them. Only safe when clients cannot reach this backend except through those proxies.
TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=

# Or: one header that the proxy in front of this backend always sets itself and never passes through from a client.
# x-forwarded-for is not accepted here.
TRUSTED_CLIENT_IP_HEADER=
